1
00:00:01,050 --> 00:00:01,958
Every autumn,

2
00:00:01,988 --> 00:00:04,900
giant blooms of jellyfish drift onto the coast.

3
00:00:07,850 --> 00:00:09,070
At a nuclear plant,

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:11,693
they can choke the seawater intakes in hours.

5
00:00:12,187 --> 00:00:13,309
Around the world,

6
00:00:13,339 --> 00:00:14,878
plants have lost power to them,

7
00:00:14,908 --> 00:00:16,471
even with early warning.

8
00:00:17,750 --> 00:00:21,062
Today's answer is still boats, nets and crews.

9
00:00:22,950 --> 00:00:24,175
This is JAZR.

10
00:00:24,687 --> 00:00:26,662
One button after the alert.

11
00:00:27,175 --> 00:00:28,350
No boats.

12
00:00:30,350 --> 00:00:32,330
A moving-belt screen sweeps the swarm

13
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,940
along its face into high-flow entrances.

14
00:00:35,435 --> 00:00:37,794
Anything that slips past meets Layer 2:

15
00:00:37,825 --> 00:00:40,074
a hydro-jet curtain, no air,

16
00:00:40,104 --> 00:00:41,765
lifting it into a skimmer.

17
00:00:42,850 --> 00:00:45,345
A turtle grid lets wildlife escape.

18
00:00:45,839 --> 00:00:47,108
Our HydroLift floats

19
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:48,812
jellyfish up with the water.

20
00:00:49,307 --> 00:00:50,773
Nothing touches them.

21
00:00:51,268 --> 00:00:54,253
Oxygenated, they travel by gravity pipe.

22
00:00:55,350 --> 00:00:57,758
A ten-day drift forecast picks the outlet,

23
00:00:57,788 --> 00:01:00,420
and they're released alive, ten kilometres away,

24
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:02,387
where the sea won't bring them back.

25
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:05,995
Operators run it all from the Bloom Incident OS:

26
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:08,970
live process control, hard-wired interlocks,

27
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,938
and AI advice that never takes a safety action.

28
00:01:14,350 --> 00:01:16,416
And this isn't a concept slide.

29
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:19,111
It's validated against our physics model,

30
00:01:19,141 --> 00:01:20,716
stress-tested with over six hundred

31
00:01:20,746 --> 00:01:21,966
engineering checks,

32
00:01:21,996 --> 00:01:24,049
a hundred and twelve automated tests,

33
00:01:24,079 --> 00:01:26,010
and real Gulf ocean data.

34
00:01:26,506 --> 00:01:28,130
In our live simulation,

35
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:29,956
about ninety-nine percent of the bloom

36
00:01:29,986 --> 00:01:32,052
is kept off the plant's screens.

37
00:01:33,850 --> 00:01:36,983
Next: a tank test with real surrogate jellyfish,

38
00:01:37,013 --> 00:01:38,737
then a one-lane pilot.

39
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,272
JAZR.

40
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,937
The plant keeps running.

41
00:01:44,487 --> 00:01:46,048
The sea keeps living.

42
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:50,308
Engineered at IIT Delhi, Abu Dhabi.

